        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-31T23:10:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, though since we don\u0027t allow structs to be uniforms in RTEs, the error message in a RTE is currently `variables of type \u0027struct InvalidStruct1\u0027 may not be uniform` without the \"caused by\" line (i.e. we reject the struct without recursion over its fields). If we want to maintain that behavior, then this should check `!IsRuntimeEffect` here too.\n\nThat would work but I think the condition becomes less self-contained since it will make assumptions on when `check_valid_uniform_type` logs its errors. I personally prefer to keep all of this logging logic in one place, so either in `check_valid_uniform_type` as it is now or here at the call site as it was in the first patch set.\n\nThat said, I went ahead and changed the `level` recursion count to a boolean flag and added a comment to make it less cryptic.",
      "parentUuid": "6ffe8c28_dac360d0",
